\code{ci_method = "bca"} adds a leave-one-subject-out jackknife on top --- one
further fit per subject. On the paper's \code{slpower1}, 200 participants, a
default BCa bootstrap is roughly a minute and a half; on \code{slpower3}, whose
model is slower to fit, nearer two and a half. Pass a small \code{R} while setting
a calculation up, and leave the default for the answer you intend to report.
